# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Port packs carry DELIBERATE CRLF bytes. Do not let Git normalise them away.
#
# Windows `main` stores src/main_window.py, src/ui/components/sidebar.py and
# src/ui/html/sidebar.html with CRLF endings, so the hunks that touch those
# files are generated with CR bytes on every context and +/- line. `git apply`
# matches context byte-exactly, so if Git strips the CRs on commit
# (core.autocrlf=input does exactly that) the pack still applies on Linux but
# FAILS on Windows with "patch does not apply" - and the corruption is
# invisible, because the diff renders identically either way.
#
# `-text` marks these as binary: no conversion on commit or on checkout.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.diff  -text
*.patch -text
